{"availability":"available","full":"rav4nn/agent-chrome","name":"agent-chrome","description":"Your Chrome, behind the terminal. Claude Code drives a copy of your signed-in Chrome in a window that opens behind your apps and never takes focus. macOS.","category":"Developer tools","language":"JavaScript","stars":3,"forks":1,"created":"2026-09-30T17:15:18Z","updated":"2026-10-02T09:27:23Z","license":"MIT","branch":"main","homepage":"https://agentchrome.hardeep.cv","topics":["browser-automation","cdp","chrome","chrome-devtools-mcp","claude-code","claude-code-plugin","macos","mcp"],"demo":null,"color":"#63362a","ink":"#f8c7a8","lastCheckedAt":"2026-10-03T09:36:58.563Z","lastAttemptAt":"2026-10-03T09:36:58.563Z","lastAvailableAt":"2026-10-03T09:36:58.563Z","lastDemoCheckedAt":"2026-10-03T09:36:58.563Z","discoveredVia":[],"metrics":[{"at":"2026-10-03T09:36:58.563Z","stars":3,"forks":1}],"technologies":[],"overview":{"kind":"readme","version":1,"paragraphs":["agent-chrome lets Claude Code use a copy of your signed-in Chrome. The window opens behind your other apps, so you keep typing while Claude browses as you.","Website Install How it works Watch the 1:26 video","Same prompt, two setups. Playwright MCP pulls Chrome to the front on every call, and what you type next lands in the browser. agent-chrome opens the tabs in a red window behind your terminal. Focus stays where you left it."],"features":["Request-ID remapping. Each client numbers its requests 1, 2, 3, ... on its own, and those ids would collide on the pipe. The proxy rewrites every incoming id to a unique proxy id, records proxyId → {client, originalId,…","Cached target state. The proxy turns on target discovery and auto-attach itself and caches every target and session. When a client asks for discovery or auto-attach, the proxy replays the cache to that client instead of…","Shared sessions. Chrome's events go to every client. Clients ignore events for sessions they don't track."],"sourceUrl":"https://github.com/rav4nn/agent-chrome/blob/main/README.md","fingerprint":"c29723cdfa411342ad2992499792e6881f924836c9d1797a3d74a8aaf590b40c","extractedAt":"2026-10-03T09:36:58.563Z"},"overviewCheckedAt":"2026-10-03T09:36:58.563Z","projectInsights":{"version":1,"whatItDoes":{"text":"agent-chrome lets Claude Code use a copy of your signed-in Chrome. The window opens behind your other apps, so you keep typing while Claude browses as you.","sourceUrl":"https://github.com/rav4nn/agent-chrome/blob/main/README.md"},"audience":[],"requirements":[{"kind":"account","status":"required","text":"So two Claude sessions either fight over the profile lock or each start a throwaway Chrome, and you sign in again every session.","sourceUrl":"https://github.com/rav4nn/agent-chrome/blob/main/README.md"},{"kind":"account","status":"required","text":"If it stops at a login, a 2FA code or a CAPTCHA, you click in and finish that step yourself.","sourceUrl":"https://github.com/rav4nn/agent-chrome/blob/main/README.md"}],"fingerprint":"c29723cdfa411342ad2992499792e6881f924836c9d1797a3d74a8aaf590b40c","sourceUrl":"https://github.com/rav4nn/agent-chrome/blob/main/README.md","checkedAt":"2026-10-03T09:36:58.563Z"},"overviewRepoUpdated":"2026-10-02T09:27:23Z","readmeSnapshot":{"version":1,"status":"saved","sourceUrl":"https://github.com/rav4nn/agent-chrome/blob/main/README.md","checkedAt":"2026-10-03T09:36:58.563Z","hash":"c29723cdfa411342ad2992499792e6881f924836c9d1797a3d74a8aaf590b40c","originalBytes":20255,"storedBytes":20255,"truncated":false,"searchTerms":["chrome","proxy","claude","window","agent-chrome","profile","one","copy","add","agent","every","mcp","open","session","tab","plugin","port","work","each","same","sessions","behind","browser","chrome-devtools-mcp","code","default","it.","new","only","own","real","uses","doesn","macos","nbsp","playwright","quit","two","what","when","which","cli","client","how","name","off","over","pipe","run","see","signed","while","about","chrome-work","chrome.","does","google",